--
N5008 [temp.deduct.call]/1-4 + [temp.variadic]/4: a variadic function template
with a forwarding-reference parameter pack `A&&...` deduces each pack element
independently, and the elements may have distinct types; the instantiated
function then has one parameter per element with its own type.  CBMC expanded
the pack into pack_size copies of the FIRST element's parameter (correct only
for a homogeneous pack), so for a forwarding-reference pack a later argument of
a different type could not bind and the call was wrongly rejected as "found no
match".  Fixed in cpp_typecheck_resolvet::guess_function_template_args by
assigning each expanded parameter its corresponding deduced pack-element type.
Reduced (via cvise, keeping real headers) from src/util/validate_expressions.cpp
`call_on_expr<...>(ns, vm)`.  assertion.3 provides non-vacuity.
